1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:06,650
Meet FSQ. Describe a goal, test the real app, and inspect the evidence.

2
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:13,300
This is the FSQ web interface, launched with the fsq ui command.

3
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:20,400
On the left, a real Android phone is mirrored so you can follow the test.

4
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:23,200
Open Quick Test.

5
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,200
Select Android.

6
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,400
Choose the connected Pixel 6.

7
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:34,750
Describe the task in natural language: open Edge and find the FSQ GitHub repository.

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:39,150
Then follow the link in its About section to the website.

9
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:45,150
Specify what to verify: Describe a goal, and Test the real app.

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,650
Then, start the test.

11
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:53,200
FSQ begins executing the task on the connected Android phone.

12
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:55,950
It opens Edge.

13
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:01,650
It searches for the repository, just as a user would.

14
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:05,600
Then it opens the FSQ repository.

15
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:12,750
The activity timeline shows the actions. Captured screenshots provide a record of what happened.

16
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:16,850
The website opens. Next, check the expected content.

17
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:26,350
FSQ checks for the two phrases in the test goal: Describe a goal, and Test the real app.

18
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:30,600
The recorded assertion passes.

19
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:36,450
The run reports success, with a summary of the verification result.

20
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:43,650
Review the captured screens to see how the task progressed.

21
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:45,900
Open the report.

22
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:51,650
Inspect the execution status, verification result, and evidence availability.

23
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:57,650
Explore the recorded actions and structured logs for more detail.

24
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:03,000
From a natural-language goal to a test result you can inspect.

25
00:02:04,008 --> 00:02:09,658
Ready to try your own test? Visit the FSQ website to get started.

